    <span class="cow-cat-zone cow-cat-zone-left"></span><span class="cow-cat-zone cow-cat-zone-center"></span><span class="cow-cat-zone cow-cat-zone-right"></span>
  </section>
  <div class="home-content">
    <h1>Electronic Structure Atlas</h1>
    <p class="lede">Understand the physical and conceptual structure of electronic-structure research.</p>
    <p><strong>Research path.</strong> Scientific question → target observable → physical model → electronic-structure theory → computational method → numerical representation → calculation → validated observable → scientific interpretation.</p>
    <ul class="section-list">
      <li><a href={href('/core/')}>Core</a> — follow the continuous explanation from the quantum problem of matter to calculations, properties, response, and spectra.</li>
      <li><a href={href('/theory/')}>Foundations</a> — repair or connect a prerequisite when it interrupts the Core argument.</li>
      <li><a href={href('/reading/')}>Reading</a> — follow a continuous source or open a research paper.</li>
      <li><a href={href('/methods/')}>Methods</a> — understand solution strategies and their limits.</li>
      <li><a href={href('/index/')}>Atlas Index</a> — find any public page with the browser’s Find command.</li>
      <li><a href="https://maxwell3919.github.io/DFT-Research-Workflow/">DFT Research Workflow</a> — execute, converge, validate, interpret, and preserve a calculation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="secondary">Supporting resources: <a href={href('/computational-tools/')}>Computational Tools</a> under Methods and the normalized <a href={href('/reference/')}>Reference</a> collection.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
